# Optional ML core runtime
# Cross-platform deterministic ML feature baseline.
# This file must remain installable on supported CI + local platforms.
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core.txt
#
# PLATFORM MATRIX (ADR-032):
#   OS:    Darwin (macOS), Linux
#   ISA:   arm64 (Apple Silicon), x86_64 (Intel/AMD)
#   Accel: cpu (default), mps (macOS ARM64), cuda (Linux x86_64)
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Lockfiles must be compiled per-platform / per-index policy
# - CPU-only lockfiles should use the PyTorch CPU index in compilation
# - This layer EXCLUDES platform-specific packages (rawpy, coremltools)
# - This layer EXCLUDES SAM2 due to build-time torch requirements
# - Accel is EXPLICIT via profile, never inferred from OS
#
# SECURITY NOTE (CVE-2025-32434):
# - torch < 2.6.0 has a critical RCE vulnerability (CVSS 9.8) via torch.load()
# - macOS Intel (x86_64) is DEPRECATED: no official torch 2.6.0+ wheels exist
# - macOS ARM64 and Linux use torch 2.6.0+ (secure versions)
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (deterministic, platform-aware) ---
# Pinned for known-good SAM2/CLIP determinism stack
#
# SECURITY: torch 2.6.0+ required to patch CVE-2025-32434 (torch.load RCE)
#
# Platform-specific version notes:
# - macOS Intel (x86_64): NOT SUPPORTED - no torch 2.6.0+ wheels available
# - macOS Apple Silicon (arm64): torch 2.6.0 (secure, MPS support)
# - Linux (all arch): torch 2.6.0 (secure, CPU/CUDA support)
#
# NOTE: When updating torch versions, verify SAM2/CLIP compatibility.

# macOS Intel (DEPRECATED - no secure torch wheels available)
# WARNING: No official torch 2.6.0+ wheels exist for macOS x86_64.
# This platform is NO LONGER SUPPORTED for ML workloads.
# Users must migrate to macOS ARM64 (Apple Silicon) or Linux.
# Installation on macOS Intel will fail with a clear dependency resolution error.

# macOS Apple Silicon (MPS) - SECURE
torch>=2.6.0,<3 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # CVE-2025-32434 patched
torchvision>=0.21.0,<1 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # matches torch 2.6.0+

# Linux (CPU/CUDA baseline) - SECURE
torch>=2.6.0,<3 ; platform_system == "Linux"  # CVE-2025-32434 patched
torchvision>=0.21.0,<1 ; platform_system == "Linux"  # matches torch 2.6.0+

